-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura: adic Galois representation at a Hecke point
-- statement:
--   The assertion is a closed $\forall$-statement. Let $p$ be a prime, $N$ a nonzero level, $S$ a finite set of natural numbers with $p \in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $N$, and let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal) with finite residue field, in which $p$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\ N\ 2\ S$ — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ — to $\mathcal{O}'$. Then there is a type $\mathcal{O}''$ carrying the same kind of structure (characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field) together with an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra structure making it module-finite over $\mathcal{O}'$ with local structure map, such that $\mathcal{O}' \to \mathcal{O}''$ is injective, and there exists $\rho \in \mathrm{GaloisRepAdic}\ \mathcal{O}''$, i.e. a free $\mathcal{O}''$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (realised as the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$) to $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}''}(V)$ which is adically continuous (for each $n$ some finite subextension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ has the property that all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise act trivially on $V$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}^n V$), with the following two properties. First, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$, the coefficient being the image of $\chi(T_\ell)$ in $\mathcal{O}''$. Second, for every prime $q$ with $q \nmid N$ and $q \neq p$, $\rho$ is unramified at $q$: for every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit, every element of the image of its inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ acts as the identity on $V$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura construction in the form needed here: every $\mathcal{O}'$-valued point of the weight-$2$, level-$N$ Hecke algebra with the primes in $S$ removed is carried by a two-dimensional adic Galois representation whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials are the expected ones. It is the Galois-representation input to the assembly of Hecke–Galois data at each level, and through those data to the modularity-lifting step.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_galoisRep_of_point.lean

